; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.329
;; What TS 29.329's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: the notes under the commands of clause 6.1, then the AVP
;; clauses of 6.3. The information-element tables of the commands, and the
;; procedures, are TS 29.328's. A clause pointing at another document for a
;; layout is an `element`; a rule depending on a feature is `text-only`.


;; The notes under the commands of clause 6.1. Neither node is told how the
;; other's support of the feature is known.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pur-data-reference-update-eff-enhance
; AVP: Data-Reference
; Command: Profile-Update-Request
; Section: 6.1.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"NOTE: More than one Data-Reference AVP may be present in the message only if both the AS and the HSS support the Update-Eff-Enhance feature."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pua-data-reference-update-eff-enhance
; AVP: Data-Reference
; Command: Profile-Update-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"NOTE: The Data-Reference AVP may be present in the message only if both the AS and the HSS support the Update-Eff-Enhance feature."
    text-only


;; Clause 6.2: an answer carrying one of the clause's result codes, its
;; own and those it lists from TS 29.229, carries it in
;; Experimental-Result and no Result-Code.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: uda-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: User-Data-Answer
; Section: 6.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_NOT_RECOGNIZED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_READ or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_MODIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_NOTIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_TOO_MUCH_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = "DIAMETER_ERROR_TRANSPARENT_DATA OUT_OF_SYNC" or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_SUBS_DATA_ABSENT or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_NO_SUBSCRIPTION_TO_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_DSAI_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_IDENTITIES_DONT_MATCH or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_USER_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_PRIOR_UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pua-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Profile-Update-Answer
; Section: 6.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_NOT_RECOGNIZED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_READ or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_MODIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_NOTIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_TOO_MUCH_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = "DIAMETER_ERROR_TRANSPARENT_DATA OUT_OF_SYNC" or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_SUBS_DATA_ABSENT or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_NO_SUBSCRIPTION_TO_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_DSAI_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_IDENTITIES_DONT_MATCH or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_USER_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_PRIOR_UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sna-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Subscribe-Notifications-Answer
; Section: 6.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_NOT_RECOGNIZED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_READ or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_MODIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_NOTIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_TOO_MUCH_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = "DIAMETER_ERROR_TRANSPARENT_DATA OUT_OF_SYNC" or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_SUBS_DATA_ABSENT or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_NO_SUBSCRIPTION_TO_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_DSAI_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_IDENTITIES_DONT_MATCH or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_USER_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_PRIOR_UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pna-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Push-Notification-Answer
; Section: 6.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_NOT_RECOGNIZED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_READ or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_MODIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_DATA_CANNOT_BE_NOTIFIED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_TOO_MUCH_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = "DIAMETER_ERROR_TRANSPARENT_DATA OUT_OF_SYNC" or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_SUBS_DATA_ABSENT or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_NO_SUBSCRIPTION_TO_DATA or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_DSAI_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_IDENTITIES_DONT_MATCH or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_USER_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE or Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_PRIOR_UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS


;; The AVP clauses of 6.3.
;; "Either ... or" is one of the three: that no two are present has no
;; members form.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-identity-one-identity
; AVP: User-Identity
; Section: 6.3.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"This AVP contains either a Public- Identity AVP or an MSISDN AVP or an External-Identifier AVP."
    members at-least-one Public-Identity MSISDN External-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: msisdn-e164
; AVP: MSISDN
; Section: 6.3.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"This AVP contains an MSISDN, in international number format as described in ITU-T Rec E.164 [8], encoded as a TBCD-string, i.e. digits from 0 through 9 are encoded 0000 to 1001; 1111 is used as a filler when there is an odd number of digits; bits 8 to 5 of octet n encode digit 2n; bits 4 to 1 of octet n encode digit 2(n-1)+1."
    encoding e164-tbcd


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-data-element
; AVP: User-Data
; Section: 6.3.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"The exact content and format of this AVP is described in 3GPP TS 29.328 [1] Annex C as Sh-Data."
    encoding element TS29.328 C "Sh-Data"


;; A Wildcarded PSI and a Wildcarded IMPU are both text a single message
;; does not tell apart.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: wildcarded-public-identity-psi
; AVP: Wildcarded-Public-Identity
; Section: 6.3.19
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"This AVP only contains a Wildcarded PSI over Sh interface."
    text-only


;; The sentence follows ONE_TIME_NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED (0); the AVP is
;; carried in SNR alone, beside the Data-Reference values UEReachabilityForIP
;; (25) names.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: snr-one-time-notification
; AVP: One-Time-Notification
; Command: Subscribe-Notifications-Request
; Section: 6.3.22
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"This AVP is only applicable to UE reachability for IP (25)"
    requires Data-Reference = 25


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pre-paging-supported-default
; AVP: Pre-paging-Supported
; Section: 6.3.26
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"If this AVP is not present in the command, the default value is PREPAGING_NOT_SUPPORTED (0)."
    default PREPAGING_NOT_SUPPORTED


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: udr-flags-undefined-bits
; AVP: UDR-Flags
; Section: 6.3.28
; Table: 6.3.28/1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender of the request and discarded by the receiver of the request."
    bits only 0 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: call-reference-number-element
; AVP: Call-Reference-Number
; Section: 6.3.30
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"The exact content and format of this AVP is described in 3GPP TS 29.002 [11]."
    encoding element TS29.002 17.7.3 "CallReferenceNumber"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: as-number-element
; AVP: AS-Number
; Section: 6.3.31
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.1.0
"The exact content and format of this AVP corresponds to the gmsc-address parameter described in 3GPP TS 29.002 [11]."
    encoding element TS29.002 17.7.8 "ISDN-AddressString"
